do_1 = "For each query, take baseline candidates plus known evidence, ask the teacher to answer with the set, judge sufficiency, then prune by leave-one-out to a minimal sufficient set; record per-item necessity, a graded utility score per item, teacher identity, prompt version and judge outcome. For bucket queries the reference is the recorded next action; exclude and count queries whose reference the teacher cannot reproduce."
do_2 = "Use weak lexical labels and gold evidence to order pruning so that calls are spent where the outcome is uncertain. Make the campaign resumable and idempotent with a valid partial output at every point."
do_3 = "test_3_1.py runs the labeller on a fake teacher whose behaviour encodes a known minimal set and proves it is recovered, kills and resumes a campaign, and checks the cost estimate against actual spend."
